      "message": "Hi Jerome, the bug is in the unit test, not the encoder change. The fix itself it correct. I checked the failing builds, it forces the FORCE_HIGHBITDEPTH_DECODING\u003d1, so the decoder returns 16-bit images for an 8-bit stream. The encoder recon from AV1_GET_NEW_FRAME_IMAGE stays 8-bit, and MD5::Add() hashes 2 bytes per sample for high bitdepth images, so the hashes can never match.\n\nI can create a fix, init the test decoder with allow_lowbitdepth \u003d 1, like encode_test_driver.cc does.\n\nInstead of reverting, could I send a small follow-up that fixes only the test? I can upload it today.",
